[01:02] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'of truth. And stick around because I want to show you a genuinely useful open- source tool that was built exactly this way. Think about how most people use an AI coder today. You describe a feature in chat, it writes some code, you course correct, it forgets, you'

[01:16] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'repeat, and three hours later, you\'re not even sure what you actually built. That is vibe coding, and it falls apart the moment a project gets real. Spec driven development flips it. You align on the plan first in writing, and the AI'

[01:28] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: A slide comparing "VIBE CODING" with "SPEC-DRIVEN" development methodologies.
AUDIO: 'executes against that plan. Same speed, far less chaos, and an actual paper trail of every decision you made. Picture asking for a login form, getting one, then two features later, the AI'

[01:41] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'quietly rewrites your validation and breaks it because nothing ever wrote the rules down. With a spec, those rules are pinned down once and the assistant has to respect them on every future change instead of quietly forgetting them the'

